# Next.js + Supabase conventions

## Architecture

- **Server Components** fetch data (`getWorkshopSignups` in page, wrapped in Suspense)
- **Client Components** only for interactivity (`RegisterForm` with `useActionState`)
- **Server Actions** in `src/lib/actions/` with `"use server"` — validate with Zod, call `revalidatePath`
- **Supabase server client** via `@supabase/ssr` in `src/lib/supabase/server.ts` — never import in Client Components

## Do

- Colocate action types with actions (`RegisterState`)
- Use `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` for URL/anon key; never expose service role key
- Handle missing env gracefully (`isSupabaseConfigured()`)
- Wrap async server UI in `<Suspense>` with a skeleton fallback

## Don't

- Fetch Supabase in Client Components for initial data
- Put secrets in `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` vars
- Skip validation in Server Actions — always validate `FormData` server-side

## Files

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `src/lib/supabase/server.ts` | Server-only Supabase client |
| `src/lib/actions/workshop-signups.ts` | Server Actions |
| `src/app/register/page.tsx` | Server page + Suspense |
| `src/components/register-form.tsx` | Client form |
| `supabase/migrations/` | SQL schema |
